<mujoco model="parcel_city_block_b">
  <!-- ============================ HELD OUT ============================
       Card W-1 (2026-08-21). This scene EXISTS SO THAT A GENERALIZATION
       CLAIM CAN BE MADE. It is a different block: the street runs north-south
       instead of east-west, the sidewalks, crossing, buildings, furniture and
       pedestrians are all in different places, and every material is a
       different texture from `city_block.xml`. What it deliberately keeps is
       the SEMANTIC VOCABULARY - the same eight classes, the same geom-name
       prefixes - so `configs/scenes/city_block.semantics.yaml` reads it without
       a second sidecar and a claim measured here is a claim about the same
       question asked of unseen pixels.

       THE RULE, and it is enforced by a test, not by good intentions:
       **no perception component may be developed, tuned, thresholded or
       measured against this scene outside a declared held-out evaluation.**
       `tests/test_held_out_scene.py` enumerates every file in the repo that
       mentions `city_block_b` and reddens if that set is not exactly the
       declared allowlist. Card W-1 itself never ran a detector or a VLM on it:
       the only thing W-1 measured here is geometry (its scene-truth artifact).

       Physics note: this scene has no frozen baseline behind it, so the
       byte-equivalence argument that protects `city_block.xml` does not apply
       and is not claimed. The `vis_*` naming rule still holds - every geom
       added for looks is non-colliding and massless - so that a future eval
       driving a robot here gets the same "visuals never touch physics"
       guarantee.
       ================================================================= -->
  <include file="../../../third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/go2.xml"/>
  <compiler meshdir="../../../third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/assets"
    texturedir="assets/textures"
    angle="radian" autolimits="true"/>

  <statistic center="0 0 0.4" extent="8"/>

  <visual>
